# For a fixed row i, each U entry A[i, j] with j >= i depends only on:
#   - A[i, k] for k < i (the current row of L), and
#   - A[k, j] for k < i (previous rows of U),
# all of which are fully computed before row i. Therefore, different
# columns j at the same i have no loop-carried dependences and can
# be computed in parallel.
#
# We:
#   1) shift the U j-loop to start at 0 so its extent is (n - i),
#   2) tile that j-loop by a constant factor for cache locality,
#   3) parallelize the outer tile loop with OpenMP,
#   4) simplify and rename the resulting procedure.

